---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { breadcrumbBlock } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'Privacy Policy – RaidCalc';
const description =
  'RaidCalc privacy: no accounts, no analytics cookies, no upload of your raid plans. Plans live in your browser’s local storage. Plain-language summary first.';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Privacy' }];
const updated = '2026-10-11';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/privacy/" crumbs={crumbs}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbBlock([{ name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' }])]}
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="value-line">Short version: RaidCalc collects almost nothing, and your raid plans never leave your device.</p>
      <p class="source-note" style="margin-top:8px">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Plain-language summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No account, no sign-up</strong> - we don’t know who you are and don’t want to.</li>
        <li><strong>Your raid plans stay local.</strong> Targets, quantities and sides are saved in your browser’s local storage so the three tools can hand off. That data never leaves your device and is never transmitted to us.</li>
        <li><strong>No tracking cookies, no ads, no fingerprinting.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>No selling data.</strong> There is no data to sell.</li>
        <li>If we ever add privacy-friendly, aggregate analytics (e.g. page-view counts without identifiers), this page will be updated first and the change dated.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the site stores on your device</h2>
      <p>
        One localStorage key, <span class="mono">raidcalc.plan.v1</span>, containing your picked targets and
        quantities - for example <span class="mono">[{"{"}"t":"sheet-door","q":2{"}"}]</span>. It exists so the
        calculator, solver and farming ETA share one plan. You can erase it any time with the “Clear plan” button
        or by clearing site data in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing beyond standard, anonymous server logs our host (Cloudflare) keeps for security and abuse
        prevention - IP addresses and request metadata processed under Cloudflare’s privacy policy. We don’t run
        Google Analytics or equivalent trackers.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Rust is rated mature; this site is intended for the game’s audience and collects no personal information from anyone, of any age.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Because no personal data is collected, there is generally nothing to export or delete. If you believe we
        hold personal data about you (e.g. from an email you sent), write to
        <a href="mailto:hello@raidcalc.top" class="mono">hello@raidcalc.top</a> and we will handle it under GDPR/DPDP
        principles: access, correction, deletion.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>Material changes to this policy will be dated at the top of this page and noted in the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
